WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.885
This is one order,
recorded start to finish

2
00:00:02.925 --> 00:00:06.185
on the live AgenticOrg service,
with a test payment.

3
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:08.739
A shop owner sets up a shop,

4
00:00:08.906 --> 00:00:12.023
a buyer's AI assistant
finds it and builds the order,

5
00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:15.616
and the buyer pays the shop
on the shop's own payment page.

6
00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:19.848
The merchant opens Sell everywhere

7
00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:22.696
and picks their new shop, Kaveri Coffee.

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.554
They have already saved the keys
of their own Plural account,

9
00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:28.853
in sandbox mode for this recording.

10
00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:34.067
The shop has no Shopify store,
so it uploads a spreadsheet:

11
00:00:34.218 --> 00:00:36.890
two coffees, with prices and stock.

12
00:00:38.519 --> 00:00:41.005
Next come the policies buyers will see,

13
00:00:41.045 --> 00:00:43.831
and a flat shipping fee
of forty-nine rupees

14
00:00:43.871 --> 00:00:45.283
for orders within India.

15
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:50.622
Then the limits every AI agent
must stay within:

16
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:52.004
the largest order,

17
00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:55.262
the most per day,
and the most items in one order.

18
00:00:55.848 --> 00:00:57.517
Nothing is set by default.

19
00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:03.759
For payment, AgenticOrg tests
the merchant's Plural keys,

20
00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:05.850
and the merchant chooses to take payment

21
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.537
in their own Plural account.

22
00:01:07.855 --> 00:01:10.427
AgenticOrg never holds the buyer's money.

23
00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:14.646
Last, the merchant names the shop
on the network,

24
00:01:14.686 --> 00:01:19.720
accepts the terms,
and turns Sell everywhere on.

25
00:01:20.336 --> 00:01:23.388
Shops on Shopify
add their products another way.

26
00:01:23.961 --> 00:01:25.487
In the Shopify admin,

27
00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:28.661
they create an app
that can read products and stock,

28
00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:32.289
then paste the store address
and the app's access token here.

29
00:01:32.623 --> 00:01:34.937
AgenticOrg then reads the products,

30
00:01:34.977 --> 00:01:36.977
prices and stock by itself.

31
00:01:37.965 --> 00:01:41.614
Their buyers can also pay
in the shop's own Shopify checkout,

32
00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.018
instead of Plural.

33
00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.044
A few minutes later,
the web address has its certificate,

34
00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:49.516
and the shop is live.

35
00:01:50.104 --> 00:01:53.022
AI apps such as ChatGPT and Claude,

36
00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:55.468
the AgenticOrg bot on Telegram,

37
00:01:55.609 --> 00:01:57.408
and the open web can reach it,

38
00:01:57.448 --> 00:02:00.197
and buyers pay
on the shop's own Plural page.

39
00:02:00.796 --> 00:02:04.251
Google, Microsoft and Perplexity
are still to come.

40
00:02:06.742 --> 00:02:08.122
Now the buyer's side.

41
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.100
A simple console stands in
for the buyer's AI assistant,

42
00:02:12.244 --> 00:02:15.175
and makes the same live calls
an AI app makes.

43
00:02:15.774 --> 00:02:18.446
The buyer wants two packs
of filter coffee,

44
00:02:18.591 --> 00:02:20.072
delivered to Bengaluru.

45
00:02:22.437 --> 00:02:25.362
It lists the shops
on the network and searches them,

46
00:02:25.402 --> 00:02:27.785
and finds the merchant's filter coffee

47
00:02:27.825 --> 00:02:29.825
at four hundred and twenty rupees.

48
00:02:30.587 --> 00:02:32.812
It opens a checkout for two packs,

49
00:02:32.959 --> 00:02:35.782
then adds the buyer's name
and delivery address.

50
00:02:36.245 --> 00:02:38.564
The shop offers its flat shipping rate,

51
00:02:38.715 --> 00:02:42.244
and the total comes
to eight hundred and eighty-nine rupees.

52
00:02:42.855 --> 00:02:46.521
The checkout is ready,
so the agent asks to complete it.

53
00:02:47.107 --> 00:02:50.295
AgenticOrg checks the order
against the merchant's limits

54
00:02:50.335 --> 00:02:53.209
and the verified catalog,
records the decision,

55
00:02:53.347 --> 00:02:56.288
and returns a link
to the merchant's payment page.

56
00:02:56.628 --> 00:02:58.694
The agent cannot pay on its own.

57
00:03:02.156 --> 00:03:03.648
The buyer opens the link.

58
00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:07.329
This is a Plural checkout
under the merchant's own account,

59
00:03:07.369 --> 00:03:09.487
and the buyer pays with a test card.

60
00:03:18.348 --> 00:03:20.119
Plural sends the buyer back.

61
00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:23.441
AgenticOrg confirms the payment
with Plural,

62
00:03:23.577 --> 00:03:25.199
and the order is confirmed.

63
00:03:27.185 --> 00:03:29.056
On the merchant's Orders page,

64
00:03:29.096 --> 00:03:31.520
the paid order appears with its items,

65
00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.626
the amount,
and the delivery details the buyer gave.

66
00:03:34.666 --> 00:03:37.582
The merchant's administrators
also get an email,

67
00:03:37.622 --> 00:03:39.564
and the merchant ships the order.

68
00:03:40.363 --> 00:03:41.716
That is the whole flow.

69
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:43.854
The merchant set up once.

70
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:46.155
A buyer's AI agent found the shop

71
00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:49.077
and built the order
within the merchant's limits.

72
00:03:49.543 --> 00:03:51.880
And the buyer paid the merchant directly.
